Local configuration override
----------------------------

Any *.cf file in this directory is appended to main.cf

master.cf entries
-----------------

The contents of the master.append file in this directory are appended to
master.cf, with the master.cf syntax. An entry with the same service
name and type (the first two fields) as a master.cf entry replaces it:
Postfix uses the last entry and logs a "duplicate master.cf entry"
warning. To change an entry, copy it from the output of "postconf -Mf"
and edit the copy. Example:

    submission inet n       -       n       -       20      smtpd
        -o smtpd_sasl_auth_enable=yes
        -o smtpd_sender_restrictions=

A replaced entry is static: if the original entry depends on the module
configuration (e.g. the smtpd_sender_restrictions option of submission
services), the replaced entry no longer follows its changes.

The file is not checked: an invalid entry stops Postfix until the file
is fixed or removed.
